WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.190
- [Narrator] Behold the mighty mangrove.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.580
Renowned for its toughness
and ability to foster

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.960
sensitive marine life,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.060
they play an important
role in tropical ecosystems

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.963
all around the world and,
especially, here in Sri Lanka.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:21.080
Despite their strength, the
mangroves are being destroyed

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.450
to make room for commercial
farming operations

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.500
and development deals.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.230
But all hope is not lost,

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.697
thanks to Sri Lanka's Mangrove Master.

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:31.307
- [Narrator] Douglas has worked formally

00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:33.450
doing conservation works since 1992

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.800
and recently became the
director of a museum

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.053
dedicated to mangrove conservation.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.310
- [Narrator] In addition
to stopping destruction,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.000
part of his conservation work involves

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.080
planting mangrove saplings
to replace the trees

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.480
that have already been lost.

